@format 1
@id media-loading.common.docket-removal
@title Docket removal
@section Media loading
@area Common
@entry removal-request
@summary Trace LDocketPathsRemove through Files rebuilding, optional replacement selection, PListClearChange, and the attached viewer/flow cleanup.
@related media-loading.common.files-selection, media-loading.common.files-clear, media-loading.common.viewer-close, media-loading.common.media-publication, media-loading.in-global-interface, media-loading.in-worklist, media-loading.in-funnel-tab
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag common
@tag removal

@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias surface = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PTabSurface
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias flow = Cadroue.UIShell.PFlow.PFlow

[removal-request] Docket removal request <input>
= A caller has resolved one or more candidate paths and calls LDocketPathsRemove.
> docket-removal

[docket-removal] Docket path removal <decision>
- Remove matching entries; only when at least one entry existed, raise LDocketChange first and then LDocketRemoved synchronously @ docket.LDocketPathsRemove(...)
? "At least one path removed" > docket-change
? "No matching path removed" > no-removal

[docket-change] Files state rebuilt before removal callback <process>
- LDocketChange invokes PListDocketHandle before LDocketRemoved, rebuilding Files rows, selection visuals, and lock state against the already-modified docket @ docket.LDocketRaise(...)
  @ list.PListDocketHandle(...)
> replacement-check

[no-removal] Removal changes nothing <output>
= LDocketChange and LDocketRemoved are not raised, so Files selection and viewer state do not change through this call.

[replacement-check] Current Files path still present <decision>
- In PListDocketRemoveHandle, test whether the current Files path is null or no longer exists in the modified docket @ list.PListDocketRemoveHandle(...)
? "Current path missing" > replacement-select
? "Current path still present" > current-kept

[replacement-select] Immediate replacement selection <process>
- Select the first remaining docket path, or null when empty; this synchronously reaches PListCurrentApply and invokes PListPathChange, so a tab-specific viewer request can start before the removal callback continues @ list.PListDocketRemoveHandle(...)
  @ list.PListSelectApply(...)
  @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> after-selection

[current-kept] No replacement selection needed <junction>
> after-selection

[after-selection] Replacement branch convergence <junction>
> clear-change

[clear-change] Removed-path notification to tab attachment <decision>
- After any replacement PListPathChange returns, PListDocketRemoveHandle invokes PListClearChange; the subscriber installed by PTabViewerAttach compares removed paths with the viewer's currently committed PViewerSourcePath @ list.PListDocketRemoveHandle(...)
  @ surface.PTabViewerAttach(...)
? "Committed viewer source was removed" > close-viewer
? "Committed viewer source was not removed" > removal-finished

[close-viewer] Viewer and flow cleared after removal <process>
- Force-close the viewer; the detailed LMediaUnload publication, viewer ownership invalidation, committed-media clearing, and empty viewer cargo sequence is Common / Viewer close @ viewer.PViewerMediaClose(...)
! Common / Viewer close shows why the backend Unloaded event queued during LMediaUnload cannot later overwrite the closed viewer.
- Clear the tab flow immediately after the forced viewer close @ flow.PFlowClear(...)
! A replacement PListPathChange can have started a new PViewerSourceOpen earlier in the same synchronous removal callback. If the old committed source was removed, this forced close can invalidate that just-started request before the caller resumes.
> viewer-cleared

[removal-finished] Removal did not close committed viewer <output>
= Files removal completed without force-closing the currently committed viewer source.

[viewer-cleared] Removed current viewer state cleared <output>
= The viewer is empty and flow is cleared; any later selection performed by the original caller can start another request.
